    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d294">

                <pb facs="0472" n="430" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg430"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 500.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-09-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 18, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Lord Russell is becoming a little sensitive
                    to the multiplication of the claims for damage done by the Alabama. A copy of
                    his note to me of the 14th instant, in reply to mine of the 24th of August, on
                    the case of the ship Nora, is now transmitted. I adjoin a copy of my answer. You
                    will judge from it of the expediency of furnishing me with new instructions.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>






